  "comment": "Jailrunner default-DENY allowlist. Only syscalls needed to run untrusted compute Python are permitted; everything else (network sockets, ptrace, mount/namespaces, module load, bpf/perf, keyctl, time-set, swap, reboot, and the 32-bit ABI) returns EPERM. Derived from a real syscall trace of the interpreter + stdlib and validated with a seccomp-BPF harness (see TEST-SECCOMP.md). Layered under --cap-drop ALL, --no-new-privileges, --network none, --read-only, --user 65534.",
